/**

@page page_exahype_extend-visualisation Extend the visualisation

\tableofcontents

Every solver writes its volumetric solution when the runner schedules a
snapshot. A tracer set writes trajectories when `dump_into_database()` is
configured, and `plot_faces()` selects additional face output.

# Face traces

An ADER-DG solver writes the two traces of selected faces into the snapshots
`<name>-face` below the output path:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
solver.plot_faces(
  "normal == faultNormal and std::abs(x(faultNormal) - faultPosition) < 0.5 * h(faultNormal)"
)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The predicate is a C++ expression on the face centre `x`, the width `h` of
the adjacent cells and the axis `normal`. Every selected face plots one point
per face node at its quadrature position, the cells between neighbouring
nodes, and per field one point field with the trace of the lower cell and one
with the trace of the upper cell, so a dynamic rupture application reads the
slip and the slip rate along its fault.

# Postprocessed fields

The hook `postprocess_updated_patch` runs on each updated patch and may
overwrite solution values. The plotter writes the named unknowns and
auxiliary variables declared by the solver; a derived quantity therefore
needs a declared auxiliary variable and a hook that computes its value.

*/
